# .NET Project Additions for CLAUDE.md

> Add these sections to your generated CLAUDE.md for .NET-specific behavior.

## .NET Build & Test

### Build Commands

```bash
# Build entire solution
dotnet build

# Build specific project
dotnet build src/MyProject/MyProject.csproj

# Build with release configuration
dotnet build -c Release

# Clean build
dotnet clean && dotnet build
```

### Test Commands

```bash
# Run all tests
dotnet test

# Run with verbosity
dotnet test -v normal

# Run specific test project
dotnet test tests/MyProject.Tests/MyProject.Tests.csproj

# Run with coverage (requires coverlet)
dotnet test --collect:"XPlat Code Coverage"
```

## .NET Coding Conventions

### File Organization

```
src/
├── MyProject.Api/           # Web API project
│   ├── Controllers/
│   ├── Models/
│   └── Program.cs
├── MyProject.Core/          # Business logic
│   ├── Services/
│   ├── Interfaces/
│   └── Entities/
└── MyProject.Infrastructure/ # Data access
    ├── Data/
    └── Repositories/

tests/
├── MyProject.Api.Tests/
├── MyProject.Core.Tests/
└── MyProject.Integration.Tests/
```

### Naming Conventions

| Type | Convention | Example |
|------|------------|---------|
| Interface | `I` prefix | `IUserService` |
| Async method | `Async` suffix | `GetUserAsync` |
| Test class | `Tests` suffix | `UserServiceTests` |
| Test method | `Method_Scenario_Expected` | `GetUser_ValidId_ReturnsUser` |

### Preferred Patterns

```csharp
// File-scoped namespaces
namespace MyProject.Api.Controllers;

// Records for DTOs
public record UserDto(int Id, string Name, string Email);

// Primary constructors (C# 12+)
public class UserService(IUserRepository repository, ILogger<UserService> logger)
{
    public async Task<User?> GetByIdAsync(int id) =>
        await repository.FindByIdAsync(id);
}

// Pattern matching
var result = response switch
{
    { IsSuccess: true } => Ok(response.Value),
    { Error: var error } => BadRequest(error),
    _ => StatusCode(500)
};
```

## .NET-Specific Routing Rules

Add to routing considerations:

**T1 - Lightweight:**
- NuGet package version checks
- Finding interface implementations
- Locating controller endpoints
- Checking for `[Authorize]` attributes

**T2+ - Complex:**
- Adding new controllers with full CRUD
- Implementing repository patterns
- Writing integration tests
- EF Core migrations
- Dependency injection setup

## Security Checks for .NET

Before committing, verify:

- [ ] No connection strings with passwords in appsettings.json
- [ ] User secrets used for local development
- [ ] `[Authorize]` on all non-public endpoints
- [ ] `[AllowAnonymous]` explicitly documented
- [ ] Input validation on all DTOs
- [ ] No SQL concatenation (use parameterized queries)
